      "writtenOn": "2026-04-13T15:01:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The issue here is that on a request it makes sense to have yes/no/maybe, but this is incompatible with the equivalence operator that is currently mostly being used in tests.\n\nThis is similar to `SkFontParameters` and `SkFontArguments`. `SkFontArguments` turns out to be quite useful to flexibly make a request (when providing font data) because all the information is needed and it is a specific request. `SkFontParameters` has turned out to be less useful because it is generally not necessary to get all the information all at once. Instead of using `SkFontParameters` there are just individual `getXXX` on `SkTypeface` to get each piece of information.\n\nApplying this to the current issue, it makes some sense to expand SkFontStyle into `SkFontRequest(Arguments)` which is like `SkFontParameters` but for making a request against a collection instead of request against a font file (though the line between these two is getting smaller). This would not have a `operator\u003d\u003d`. `SkTypeface::fontStyle` would be removed and replaced with `getWeight`, `getWidth`, `getStyle`, and `getSlant` (and of course `isSyntheticBold` and `isSyntheticOblique`) instead of adding a `SkFontRequest(Parameters)` which would be as unused as `SkFontParameters`. If adding a new thing anyway for the future, the existing SkFontStyle can just be allowed to remain as-is for now while adding the new `SkFontRequest`.",
      "parentUuid": "3ecf8e5a_29010932",
